--
-- Test Description
-- Checks response to magic packet in 1Gbits/s GMII mode
-- 
-- Functional Coverage
-- * Checks that synchronisation FF bytes can be recognised anywhere in frame
-- * Checks that magic packet only accepted if spec_add1 is repeated 16 times
-- * Checks that magic packet can be seen if not aligned to 16-bit boundary
-- 
-- Detailed Test Description
--  1. Initialise suitable wait states for the test.
--  2. Check reset values of registers and setup interrupts
--     and then enable receive in 1GM mode into a 32-bit DMA data bus.
--  3. Receive a correctly addressed frame that almost has a magic packet in it
--     and check that wol is not asserted.
--  4. Receive a correctly addressed frame that almost has a magic packet in it
--     at a non 16-bit alignment and check that wol is not asserted.
--  5. Receive a correctly addressed frame that has a magic packet but with crc
--     error and check that wol is not asserted.
--  6. Receive a correctly addressed frame that has a magic packet and check for
--     wol assertion
--  7. Receive a correctly addressed frame that has a magic packet at a non 
--     16-bit alignment and check for wol assertion
--  8. Turn off the magic packet WoL mask and receive a good frame which has
--     a magic packet. Check that the frame is received and wol is not asserted.
--  9. Receive a good frame which is not a magic packet to ensure everything
--     is OK and check the wol is not asserted.
-- 10. Set the local addresss to all F's (broadcast) and receive a good broadcast
--     frame which contains a magic packet. Check that magic packet is asseted.
-- 11. Check statistics for correct values from above tests.
--
-- ************************************************************************** --

--******************************************************************************
--  1. Initialise suitable wait states for the test.
--******************************************************************************
wait_states     0
bus_grant_delay 0



--******************************************************************************
--  2. Check reset values of registers and setup interrupts
--     and then enable receive in 100M mode into a 32-bit DMA data bus.
--******************************************************************************
apbrd(100) 00 00000000  -- check reset value of network control register
apbrd      18 00000000  -- check reset value of receive queue pointer
apbwr      18 fffffff0  -- write receive queue pointer
apbrd      18 fffffff0  -- check receive queue pointer
apbwr      B8 00010000  -- enable WoL magic packet mask
apbwr      00 00000004  -- enable receive
apbrd      24 00000000  -- check interrupt status
apbwr      28 0fffffff  -- enable all interrupts except WOL
apbrd      24 00000000  -- check interrupt status
apbwr      88 12345678  -- specific address register 1 bottom
apbwr      8C 00001111  -- specific address register 1 top
apbrd      04 00080000  -- check reset value of network config register
apbrd      08 00000006  -- check reset value of network status register
apbwr      04 00080400  -- indicate 1GM operation
apbrd      04 00080400  -- verify write to config register..
apbrdf     20 00000000  -- check contents of the receive status register and trigger reception of frame



